// sequencer(coverageDelta)
//
// Marker constraint that turns a chain output into a sequencer chain.
//
//   $0 coverageDelta      (z64): the ledger coverage delta of this milestone's past cone.
//
// It used to also carry per-chain delegation parameters (epoch length and
// freeze depth). Those are ledger constants now — identical for every
// sequencer — so the constraint carries only the per-milestone coverage.
// Once a chain is a sequencer chain it cannot lose that status; only chain
// destruction is possible, and a regular chain can never gain one later.
//
// coverageDelta is NOT immutable: it carries this milestone's coverage
// delta, computed and pinned by the attacher (same value the branch's stem
// reads for its total-coverage recurrence). On the ledger it is constrained to
// be strictly increasing over a same-slot chain predecessor (see
// _sameSlotPredecessorCase). Branches and slot-first milestones have a
// cross-slot predecessor and are therefore exempt; chain origins have no
// predecessor.
//
// The sibling chain constraint is always at index 2; the sequencer constraint
// sits at sequencerConstraintIndex (index 4). The position is pinned on the
// produced side and re-read at the fixed index on the successor.

// $0 chain predecessor input index
func _inputSameSlot : equal( txSlot, slotOfInputByIndex($0) )

// $0 chain predecessor input index. coverageDelta = arg 0 of the predecessor
// milestone's sequencer constraint (a sequencer chain output always carries it).
func _predCoverageDelta : parseInlineDataArgument(atPath(concat(pathToConsumedOutputs, $0, sequencerConstraintIndex)), 0, #sequencer)

// $0 chain predecessor input index. True iff the predecessor milestone is a
// branch (tick == 0). A branch resets the baseline.
func _predIsBranch : isZero(tickFromTimestampBytes(timestampOfInputByIndex($0)))

// $0 chain predecessor input index. The coverage value the successor must
// STRICTLY exceed:
//   - the predecessor's own coverageDelta, when the predecessor is a same-slot,
//     non-branch milestone (same baseline, same within-slot accumulation);
//   - 0 otherwise.
// The "0" arm covers every baseline-reset point: cross-slot predecessor
// (slot-first milestone, explicit baseline), branch SELF (its chain predecessor
// is always cross-slot), and a same-slot BRANCH predecessor (the post-branch
// first milestone, whose accumulation restarts on the new baseline). In all
// those cases the successor just needs to consolidate SOME coverage (> 0).
//
// Within a slot the baseline never switches to a different branch (same-slot
// branches are conflicts; two branches in one past cone share a lineage), so a
// same-slot non-branch predecessor always shares the successor's baseline and
// the two coverageDeltas are comparable.
func _effectivePredCoverage :
if(
	and(_inputSameSlot($0), not(_predIsBranch($0))),
	_predCoverageDelta($0),
	u64/0
)

// $0 chain predecessor input index, $1 self coverageDelta
// Unified anti-spam rule: every (non-origin) milestone must consolidate strictly
// more coverage than its effective predecessor — via new consumed (tag-along)
// outputs or a new endorsement. A milestone that only inflates without
// consolidating coverage is invalid. Gated by constEnforceCoverageDeltaMonotonicity
// (production = on; certain hand-built attacher tests turn it off).
func _enforceCoverageAdvance :
or(
	not(constEnforceCoverageDeltaMonotonicity),
	require(
		lessThan(uint8Bytes(_effectivePredCoverage($0)), uint8Bytes($1)),
		!!!coverage_delta_must_strictly_increase
	)
)

// $0 chain predecessor input index
// chain predecessor is on the same slot
func _sameSlotPredecessorCase :
require(
	or(sequencerFlagON(inputIDByIndex($0)), not(isZero(numEndorsements))),
	!!!sequencer_chain_predecessor_on_the_same_slot_must_be_either_a_sequencer_tx_too_or_endorse_another_sequencer_tx
)

// $0 chain predecessor input index
// chain predecessor is on a past slot
func _crossSlotPredecessorCase :
require(
	or(
		isBranchTransaction,
		not(isZero(numEndorsements)),
		not(isZero(txExplicitBaseline))
	),
	!!!sequencer_tx_has_incorrect_cross_slot_chain_predecessor_or_does_not_have_any_endorsements
)

// $0 chain predecessor input index
//
// Chain ORIGIN outputs ($0 == 0x, equivalently ChainID == 0x000…) have no
// tx-level requirement: the producing tx is a regular wallet tx (or another
// sequencer milestone spawning new chains) and baseline anchoring is the
// consumer's problem. Chain TRANSITIONS still dispatch to the
// baseline guarantee rules. Baseline direction will be possible to chose deterministically:
// - if predecessor is on the same slot, it must either be sequencer tx (it is the direction),
//   or otherwise it must have at least 1 endorsement (baseline direction is at index 0).
// - otherwise (cross slot predecessor case):
// -- on branch transaction baseline direction is itself
// -- otherwise endorsement at index 0 is the direction
// -- otherwise explicit baseline must be specified
// $0 chain predecessor input index, $1 self coverageDelta
func _sequencer :
or(
	equal($0, 0x),
	and(
		if(
		  _inputSameSlot($0),
		  _sameSlotPredecessorCase($0),
		  _crossSlotPredecessorCase
		),
		_enforceCoverageAdvance($0, $1)
	)
)

// enforces the sequencer transaction with more than 1 input not is in the pre branch consolidation ticks zone
// Checks: txTick <= constMaxTickValuePerSlot - constPreBranchConsolidationTicks
func checkPreBranchConsolidationTicks :
or(
   equal(numInputs, u64/1),
   require(
		lessOrEqualThan(
			uint8Bytes(txTick),
			sub(
				constMaxTickValuePerSlot,
				constPreBranchConsolidationTicks
			)
        ),
        !!!sequencer_transaction_violates_pre-branch_consolidation_ticks_constraint
   )
)

// $0 - coverageDelta (z64)
// chain constraint is always at index 2; this constraint is at sequencerConstraintIndex
//
// The "self is the tx's milestone output" check (selfOutputIndex == txSequencerOutputIndex)
// fires only for chain TRANSITIONS, never for chain ORIGINS. Rationale: a single tx is
// allowed to produce many new sequencer chain origins (a wallet "batch-spawn", or a
// sequencer milestone spawning new chains on request). Transitions remain capped at one
// per tx by the single-byte txSequencerOutputIndex marker.
func sequencer: and(
    or(
        and(
            selfIsProducedOutput,
            // pin the constraint position so successors and the stem can read it
            // at the fixed index.
            require(equal(selfBlockIndex, sequencerConstraintIndex), !!!sequencer_constraint_must_be_at_sequencerConstraintIndex),
            // selfChainPredInputIndex == 0x => chain origin output (no transition check needed).
            or(
                equal(selfChainPredInputIndex, 0x),
                require(equal(selfOutputIndex, txSequencerOutputIndex), !!!inconsistent_sequencer_output_index_on_transaction)
            ),
            checkPreBranchConsolidationTicks,
            // check chain's past ($0 = this milestone's coverageDelta, used by
            // the within-slot strict-increase rule)
            _sequencer( selfChainPredInputIndex, $0 )
        ),
        selfIsConsumedOutput
    )
)
